  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IPA Research Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will implement a large-scale community-level field experiment that encourage VSLAs to set up and operate as retail DF agents across rural unserved communities in Sierra Leone &#x2014; a market environment that is poorly studied. Agents will be established to offer both mobile money (via Orange Money) and bank services (via GT Bank) in 3 separate phases that span 2022-2025. This is an environment where the penetration of DFS is extremely low and retail agents are &#x201c;non-existent&#x201d; in these rural communities, but where there is latent demand for and potential for supply of DFS. The study will include two interventions meant to connect unserved communities to retail agents. First, to examine the broader impacts of retail agent expansions, we will encourage and onboard existing VSLAs as agents (VSLAs-as-agents) in randomly selected communities (Treatment I). Second, to test improvements in quality of services and consumer usage of DFS, we will additionally implement a simple, anonymized feedback mechanism that provides monthly consumer feedback&#x2014;based on digitized new user reviews or evaluations&#x2014;to retailers and the community in a random set of connected communities (Treatment II).</narrative>
  </description>
